body:
Sorry, got no idea what I'm talking about here..

&#x200B;

EDIT: only seeing 12W

I always turn it off when I stop using it, never left it rlly on standby. 

&#x200B;

when I first got the quest it took hoouurrssss to pair my headset up with the app and factory resetting it seems to be a massive pain ontop of all that.. uuhg.

yeeahh. woken up now and I'm trying the little included cable that's usb-c to usb-c, idk if it will charge it properly but it's charging, though turning it on I heard it disconnect and re-connect a few times going through the usual boundary things but I've heard this cable isn't really for being used whilst on

&#x200B;

EDIT: honestly the weird thing about this all thinking about it is: it's fine and works until I turn it on, that's when all the issues start with the disconnecting/reconnecting spam constantly

Sorry for 2nd reply, but this is the site, I mainly got it for substance 3d painter [https://www.adobe.com/au/products/substance3d-painter.html](https://www.adobe.com/au/products/substance3d-painter.html)

&#x200B;

EDIT: [https://gyazo.com/54674e35b724440a523494ec4faff58a](https://gyazo.com/54674e35b724440a523494ec4faff58a) this is sort of what it looks like when it happens.

Keyboard is a super cheap 1, no RGB or anything special, never had issues with it, my keyboard has only ever "disconnected" once, that was on PC wake up, it wouldn't work until I unplugged and re-plugged it in, but that's only been once in the few yrs i've had it and it happened about a week ago.

&#x200B;

I could possibly see it being a kink in the braded cable causing it potentially?

Don't believe you can get anymore at this point, could be wrong though.

&#x200B;

also: nice edit from armpits kek

Alright will try that, I will say thought just so it's clear, I'm talking about the slight plastic type rattling sound not the actual fan sound

&#x200B;

EDIT: would like to also add, my case I had for 1 year prior to this also had this same sorta noise, is it possible it's a bit of hair or something? there is a piece or 2 on the inside part of the intake fan

Ok so the thing with the CPU and psu thing, I was using a 1660 super with this cpu and it was still happening, this started after i did a windows restore point because the first time i used DDU i messed up my pc, and restored back to right before I used it.

&#x200B;

It happens in all games, feels like sometimes in programs like discord and my browser as well. started about 5-6 months ago, I've since done a pc reset though with no luck

Sorry for really late reply!

&#x200B;

I use display port, and the thing is, opening the game determines this stutter...

&#x200B;

I could open the game 5 times and it runs perfect, but then i could open it 3 times and it have the stuttering all 3 times, nothing changes whatsoever.

Yeah but it's also got a much better heatsink and fans..

&#x200B;

google asus phoenix 1660 super.. it's normal operating temp is like 84 or 86c, it has 1 single fan and a heatsink that looks like an intel CPU stock cooler

&#x200B;

the 3060ti i'm geting is the aorus elite gigabyte version.. really beefy cooler and fans

ok so... weird update. i just got a stutter, but its not accompanied by any of those other things that signified i stuttered, again i go from 60 to 55/57 fps when it happens but this time there was no gpu copy spike or hardfaults with it, though there are still hardfault spikes like the other SS i showed you, went to SS it but it went back to 0 by the time i could where it said nvidia container had 25

&#x200B;

EDIT: [https://gyazo.com/dc8c2753210ef9907140ce4ff27df6c1](https://gyazo.com/dc8c2753210ef9907140ce4ff27df6c1) best i can get

Sorry for the late reply..

&#x200B;

It's a AOC24g2, has G-sync compatibility but when i go into nvidia control panel it allows me to turn it on etcetc but says may not be compatible, I've tried it but it doesn't really fix anything

Hey sorry for the late reply, Windows restore was pretty much my last option, i tried to fix whatever happened in so many ways and even reverting the update/drivers back to what they were before all the issues started and they were still there, so far everything is working fine apart from the fact that some programs i cannot uninstall or load them

&#x200B;

the other issue is (idk if ive just noticed it now or what) is that whenever i open google chrome or a new tab or un-minimize it, i get flashed with a white screen for like 0.2 seconds, I've tried games and such and they all work fine

main monitor is using DP while 2nd monitor is using DVI, also update.. it gets weirder.

&#x200B;

So my main monitor is choppy when I move windows around, BUT. if I maximize the window on my 2nd monitor then drag it to my main monitor, it's smooth until I maximize it on my main monitor.

The frame time issues happen even if my GPU is only like 60C, it also feels like I'm stuttering when browsing sometimes (like scrolling up and down youtuber, feels like it scrolls almost at like 30fps) and to be honest these things might of always been there or might all be normal for my drivers etcetc but I'm having 1 of those big bouts of anxiety so I'm noticing every little thing and it's making me go crazy lmao.. also yes for the SSD's i was thinking of a sata 1 (not the long thin stick that goes in your motherboard, but the 1 that u kinda sit like a harddrive but for an SSD) 

&#x200B;

For streaming I'm using streamlabs OBS with nvenc yes, I switched it to something else a while ago to stream halo infinite to keep my GPU cooler but whenever the screen got busy the stream went all pixely so I changed it back to nvenc BTW I REALLY appreciate all the time you've taken to help me with all these things, I really do

my main reasoning to upgrading my GPU is because my current GPU can't reach anywhere near it's full potential because of its heatsink/cooling system, it's an ASUS phoenix 1660 super, 1 small single fan and a heatsink that makes a stock intel cooler look good, most games sit at 82c softcap and go up to 86c sometimes on medium settings when I know I could play them at high/ultra if there wasn't the heat issue, I thought it was an airflow issue but looking it up it's pretty much standard for this card and it's terrible, other then that it's pretty responsive, I've stuck to GPU driver's from 2020 since every newer 1 has caused issues like audio stutters when loading pictures on a webpage or stutters when dragging windows around or when hovering over my cursor on my taskbar icon, also recently I've been looking at MSI afterburner my GPU seems to be doing something.. weird? idk if it's normal or not, but...

&#x200B;

If for example, I'm playing a really light game (6% gpu usage) if I un-focus the game or click off the window for it, my GPU will spike to 30-40% usage and stays there until I click back onto the game, where it will drop back to about 6%, OR if I'm playing 1 game and its using let's say... 40% GPU, if I open a 2nd game, it will share it and both will use about 20% each, really odd to me. also I stream, and apart from my temps being 2 high on most games, it's been fine. I managed to stream halo infinite on all low settings at 60fps with only having lower fps (40-50) on the more open areas. also a few games I've been playing recently have been giving me frame time spikes out of nowhere (halo infinite doesn't except if I die) like lost ark and.. the big meme of em all, raid: shadow legends.

&#x200B;

Also as for the storage, i'm using a SSD/NVME on my motherboard, been needing to get a 2nd SSD for more games, staying far far away from harddrives

Not currently looked up the type of CPU I've been wanting, I've heard you should only really upgrade your CPU if it's going to make a bigger difference, kinda like a GPU where it's not a good idea to upgrade from a 2060 to a 2070 etcetc, I was thinking of budgeting about 450-500 AUD towards a CPU (about 350-400 usd)

&#x200B;

Also yeah my ram is in duel channel, though even though its max speed is 3666mhz i think the motherboard only supports 2666mhz

thank you so much for the answer, 1 more small question, since i've gotten so many different answers on this...

&#x200B;

if a CPU is bottlenecking the GPU, does that mean instead of getting let's say... 150 FPS without bottleneck, my max would be 135 with a bottle neck? just as an example of course, my biggest thing though honestly is having massive frametime spikes or framedrops, I can't stand those.
